---
/**
 * /pricing: THE canonical fee page. Every other property (homepage FAQ, blog
 * posts, docs, business, llms.txt) should state fees consistently with this
 * page and link here. Fee facts below mirror the live post-#1026 wording:
 * fee on volume only, taken in the surplus token, no cut of surplus anywhere.
 *
 * FAQ answers are rendered VERBATIM as the visible section body (the postbuild
 * check-faq-schema gate requires schema text to appear in visible text), so
 * edit the FAQS constants, not the markup.
 */
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro'
import { canonicalPage } from '../data/canonicalPages'
import { SOVEREIGN_CHAINS } from '../data/chains'

const { updated } = canonicalPage('/pricing/')
const sovereignNames = SOVEREIGN_CHAINS.map((c) => c.name) // Optimism, Unichain, Robinhood Chain
const sovereignList = `${sovereignNames[0]}, ${sovereignNames[1]}, and ${sovereignNames[2]}`

const FAQS = [
  {
    q: 'What does Ophis charge?',
    a: `Ophis applies a flat 0.10% (10 bps) fee on trade volume in the swap app, with a reduced 0.01% (1 bp) on same-chain stablecoin-to-stablecoin swaps. SDK and MCP integrations pay a reduced 0.05% (5 bps) partner rate. The fee is on volume only and is taken in the surplus token (the token you receive on a standard sell order). Orders are gasless: you pay no network gas on the swap itself.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the all-in cost on each chain?',
    a: `On the Ophis-operated chains, ${sovereignList}, the flat Ophis fee is the entire protocol cost and 100% of any price improvement a solver finds beyond your signed quote is returned to the trader. On the CoW-hosted chains, CoW Protocol adds its own fees on top: a 0.02% volume fee (0.003% on correlated pairs) plus 50% of quote improvement, capped at 0.98% of volume, making the fixed all-in there 0.12% standard and 0.013% on stable pairs.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Does Ophis take a cut of surplus?',
    a: `No. Ophis takes no cut of price improvement on any chain. On ${sovereignList}, 100% of the improvement is returned to the trader. On CoW-hosted chains, CoW Protocol retains 50% of quote improvement upstream before the remainder is returned.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What do integrators pay, and what can they charge?',
    a: `Integrations pay a 5 bps base rate: 0.05% of volume. The SDK sets a reduced 1 bp on same-chain stablecoin pairs; the keyless MCP charges the flat 5 bps base. Using the SDK or a manual appData build, integrators charge their own fee on top of ERC-20 orders, up to 95 bps under the default 100 bps aggregate cap, and Ophis takes 0% of the markup.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Are the APIs free?',
    a: `Yes. The public Intent API and the MCP server are free to call. The Intent API is rate-limited to 30 requests per minute per IP; partner-tier rate limits are reviewed case by case.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Are there rebates?',
    a: `Yes. Volume rebate tiers (10% to 50% by rolling 30-day volume) weight your share of a monthly WETH rebate pool, and a referral layer pays 8% or 12% of the net fee Ophis keeps, monthly in WETH, on-chain.`,
  },
]
---

<ContentPage
  title="Ophis fees and pricing"
  description="The canonical Ophis fee reference: a flat 0.10% (10 bps) on trade volume, 0.01% on same-chain stablecoin pairs, 5 bps for SDK and MCP integrations, all-in on the Ophis-operated chains."
  path="/pricing/"
  heading="Fees and pricing"
  lede="One flat fee on trade volume, no gas, no cut of surplus. This page is the canonical reference for what Ophis charges on every path and every chain."
  updated={updated}
  faqs={FAQS}
>
  <p>
    <strong>The short version:</strong> the swap app charges a flat 0.10% (10 bps) of trade volume,
    reduced to 0.01% (1 bp) for same-chain stablecoin-to-stablecoin swaps. SDK and MCP integrations
    pay a 5 bps partner rate. On the Ophis-operated chains, {sovereignList}, that fee is the all-in
    cost. The fee is taken in the surplus token, and Ophis takes no cut of surplus on any chain.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Path</th>
        <th scope="col">Standard rate</th>
        <th scope="col">Same-chain stablecoin pair</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://swap.ophis.fi/">Swap app</a></td>
        <td>0.10% (10 bps)</td>
        <td>0.01% (1 bp)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://github.com/ophis-fi/ophis/tree/main/packages/sdk">@ophis/sdk</a> integrations</td>
        <td>0.05% (5 bps)</td>
        <td>0.01% (1 bp)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/ai-agents">MCP server</a> (keyless)</td>
        <td>0.05% (5 bps)</td>
        <td>0.05% (5 bps, flat)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Intent API and MCP calls themselves</td>
        <td>Free</td>
        <td>Free</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  {FAQS.map((f) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{f.q}</h2>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>
    A 100,000 USDC trade pays 100 USDC all-in on an Ophis-operated chain ({sovereignList}, 0.10%),
    or 120 USDC fixed all-in on a CoW-hosted chain (0.12%). The same 100,000 between two
    stablecoins on one chain pays 10 USDC (Ophis-operated) or 13 USDC fixed (CoW-hosted), before
    CoW's share of any quote improvement.
  </p>

  <h2>Sources and detail</h2>
  <p>
    Chain-by-chain fee detail lives at <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/fees">docs.ophis.fi/fees</a>,
    integrator terms at <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/partners">docs.ophis.fi/partners</a> and
    <a href="https://business.ophis.fi/">business.ophis.fi</a>, rebate mechanics at
    <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/affiliate">docs.ophis.fi/affiliate</a>, and CoW Protocol's own
    fee schedule at <a href="https://docs.cow.fi/governance/fees">docs.cow.fi</a>. See also
    <a href="/supported-chains/">supported chains</a> for which chains are Ophis-operated.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
